s of methods are used to understand  infection by  ebola virus by stars 1 and stars 2  viruses  as well as malaria and what you'll find  a lot in this context of the infection  is that we can compare infection  as a result of similar viruses so for  example  we will talk about how other respiratory  viruses  that also cause severe respiratory  disease can compare to source cove2  we'll talk about the immunology what's  called the cytokine storm  both in source cove 2 but also we'll  talk about  ebola which as you know is one of the  pin  and pandemics that was  start of this massive scale next  generation sequencing effort so we'll  learn  some about ebola there as well but we'll  also talk about  how such transcriptomic data is being  utilized  in the context of clinical and  biomedical research  in the context of epidemiology but also  in the context of drug  development so here you can see some  examples of how  network analysis and enrichment analysis  can help us understand  the different types of responses and  targets  ultimately as nodes in those networks  that can help identify  compounds protein protein interactions  and various transmission prevention  techniques  so that we can understand the molecular  drivers or components that  help explain some of those  considerations so after you complete  this program  you will have the opportunity to speak  about  the transcriptomic methods when you read  papers you'll understand those methods  when you explain your own analysis  you'll be confident in knowing how to  explain  why you've chosen a particular method or  what did this method do  and you'll be able to share an example  project either  from one of the projects that we provide  or a project of your own  so that you can have an experience of  applying bioinformatics techniques to  a data set and kind of going through the  full process from the very beginning  of identifying that data set to then  processing the data set preparing it for  analysis and th